# Files exempt from the SPDX-header rules LIC001 and LIC002.
#
# There is exactly one reason to be on this list: the file is verbatim output of
# a third-party generator, so an `AGPL-3.0-or-later` header on it would be a
# false claim of authorship AND would displace the notice the generator's own
# licence requires to travel with it. Everything here is `cap add android`
# writing `@capacitor/cli` 8.5.1's MIT template; `apps/mobile/README.md` §2
# records that provenance and reproduces MIT's notice, which is the obligation
# this exemption exists to keep honest rather than to dodge.
#
# NOT a reason to be on this list: "the header is awkward here", "it is only
# config", "we will add it later". A file this repository authors or edits
# carries the header, and four of the twenty `cap add` wrote are therefore
# absent from this list -- AndroidManifest.xml, app/build.gradle, strings.xml
# and MainActivity.java all name this application and are all ours to maintain.
#
# Two template files are absent from this list and are NOT oversights:
# `apps/mobile/android/gradlew` and `gradlew.bat` are Gradle's own launcher
# scripts and carry no extension the header glob scans, so the rules never see
# them. Naming them here would be a LIC006 pass that proved nothing.
#
# Format: one repository-relative path per line, `#` starts a comment. Exact
# paths only -- LIC006 rejects glob syntax, rejects an absolute or `..` path,
# and rejects an entry naming a file that is not there. That last one is what
# makes the list fail closed: a generator that writes a file under a NEW name
# lands outside the list and fails LIC002 until somebody reads it.

# --- Gradle: the build the Android Gradle Plugin template supplies -----------
apps/mobile/android/build.gradle
apps/mobile/android/settings.gradle
apps/mobile/android/variables.gradle

# Rewritten by `cap sync` on every run; both carry Capacitor's own
# "DO NOT EDIT THIS FILE!" banner on line 1.
apps/mobile/android/capacitor.settings.gradle
apps/mobile/android/app/capacitor.build.gradle

# --- Android resources: template art and template layout --------------------
#
# The launcher icons are Capacitor's own artwork, which is the clearest case on
# this list: it is a creative asset under someone else's licence and relabelling
# it would be the thing §3 exists to prevent, not a formality.
apps/mobile/android/app/src/main/res/drawable-v24/ic_launcher_foreground.xml
apps/mobile/android/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_launcher_background.xml
apps/mobile/android/app/src/main/res/values/ic_launcher_background.xml
apps/mobile/android/app/src/main/res/mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher.xml
apps/mobile/android/app/src/main/res/mipmap-anydpi-v26/ic_launcher_round.xml
apps/mobile/android/app/src/main/res/layout/activity_main.xml
apps/mobile/android/app/src/main/res/values/styles.xml
apps/mobile/android/app/src/main/res/xml/file_paths.xml
